  "note": "Triennial election of the Antrim Town Commissioners, polled Wednesday 21 May 1952. There was no contest; seven members were declared elected and two seats were left to be co-opted. Wm. French and James [surname not legible] did not seek nomination (Ballymena Observer, 16 May 1952, p. 2). Seven elected unopposed for nine seats; the remaining two were to be co-opted, not elected. Returned unopposed."
